      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays have flipped the script, shedding their sluggish midsummer aura with a pair of dominant victories that scream contender grit. <strong>Blanking the Seattle Mariners 2-0 behind Dylan Cease's seven-inning, nine-strikeout masterclass</strong> last night, the Jays now sit at 42-46, third in the AL East but riding a W2 streak that's cut 11.5 games of the lead. Cease, who walked just one and allowed three hits, is the story right now - his renaissance anchoring a bullpen that's finally finding its spine, while rookie Kazuma Okamoto earned Rookie of the Month for his 54 RBIs and.295 average. The offense, though still modest, showed flashes with Vladimir Guerrero Jr. and Andrés Giménez delivering clutch hits. <strong>Today, they return to Seattle at 4:10 PM ET to continue this pivotal series, where every win could tighten the hunt for the division crown</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 4, 2026"
      },
